          "value": ""
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.5
    },
    {
      "id": "f1c4d538-0090-4a90-b090-000000000090",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -620,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 520,
        "height": 1240,
        "content": "## Automate brand monitoring on Google News into Google Sheets\n\nNo media monitoring subscription and no PR agency retainer. Every week this searches Google News for the brands and topics you are watching and appends one row per article to your sheet: headline, source, when it published, the snippet, and a link.\n\nWatch your own name and two competitors in the same sheet. Sorting by Source then shows who is getting covered where, which is the part a Google Alert email never lets you see.\n\n**Who's it for**\nFounders tracking their own coverage, comms teams watching competitors, and anyone who has given up on Google Alerts landing in a folder they never open.\n\n**How it works**\n1. A schedule trigger fires once a week\n2. One Set node holds the brands or topics you want to watch\n3. The Apify node runs one Google News search per term\n4. A Code node turns each search into one row per article\n\n**Setup**\n1. Create a free Apify account and add your API token to the Apify credential\n2. Connect your Google account in the Sheets node and pick a spreadsheet\n3. Replace the example watch terms in the config node with your brand and your competitors\n\n**Good to know**\nAbout 3 cents per watch term per week, so three terms is roughly 9 cents a week.\nGoogle News reports publication dates as relative text such as \"2 days ago\", so that is what lands in the sheet. There is no absolute date filter available, so de-duplicate on Link when you chart it.\nActor: https://apify.com/johnvc/GoogleNewsAPI?fpr=9n7kx3&fp_sid=n8n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f1c4d538-0091-4a91-b091-000000000091",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -40,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 240,
        "height": 240,
        "content": "### 1. Schedule\nRuns every Monday morning. Change the cadence, or swap in a manual trigger while you test."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
